WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.535
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.837
you know from her work on
the HBO hit series "Girls."

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.539
She stars in
the critically acclaimed series

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:09.776
"The Flight Attendant," which is
currently streaming on HBO Max.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:10.976
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.976 --> 00:00:12.345
-Take a deep breath.
-[ Gasps ]

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:13.679
-And then -- you're okay.
-No, I'm having a panic attack.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:14.847
-No, you're not having
a panic attack.

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.582
-I'm having a panic attack.
-Jessica!

00:00:16.582 --> 00:00:18.184
-Who are you --
Who is that?

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.519
You're calling your assistant?
That's Jennifer.

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:22.321
-How would you know that?
-Yep.

00:00:22.321 --> 00:00:24.124
-Jessica, grab Cassie
a Topo Chico

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.257
from the back of the fridge.

00:00:25.257 --> 00:00:27.493
-Jennifer -- Wait. Topo --
A Topo Chico?

00:00:27.493 --> 00:00:29.095
You have those on hand for me?

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.864
-I love you.
Um, they're for me.

00:00:31.864 --> 00:00:33.032
'Cause why would
they be for you?

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:35.568
'Cause, you know,
you've never been here.

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.104
-Please welcome back
to the show Zosia Mamet.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.205
♪♪

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:43.610
-Yay!

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:46.079
Hello!
Now we can touch.

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.513
We can touch.
-Okay, okay, okay.

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:48.715
-Welcome!
It's great to see you!

00:00:48.715 --> 00:00:51.117
-Thank you!
It's so good to see you, too.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:54.386
-Now, Zosia, this is --
I think this is the first time

00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:56.289
you've been --
Because you obviously have done

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:58.057
a lot of press
for this very popular show.

00:00:58.057 --> 00:00:59.425
-Yes.
-But this is the first time

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.626
anything's been in person
for you.

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.528
-This is. I actually --
I just went to wave,

00:01:02.528 --> 00:01:04.297
and then I was like,
"Nobody's there."

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:07.033
I'm waving at --
Unless there are ghosts.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.968
-We do not --
We've been trying to get ghosts.

00:01:08.968 --> 00:01:10.736
-Oh, yeah.
-Because all the shows

00:01:10.736 --> 00:01:12.305
want them.
-I know. It's so high demand.

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:14.240
-In so demand, I know.
It's okay.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.808
I heard Jimmy
has ghosts, but, yeah.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:17.443
-Yeah, Jimmy.
Well, NBC said we can only

00:01:17.443 --> 00:01:19.145
pay for ghosts for one show.
-Oh, okay. Cool, cool.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.847
-You know.
-So I didn't get them?

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:22.181
-No, sorry.
-Okay. No, that's fine.

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.950
-How -- Was it nice?
I was just talking

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.519
with Graham Norton
about how some people are happy

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:28.221
to be back doing talk shows
because it means they can

00:01:28.221 --> 00:01:30.155
just, like,
have a reason to go out.

00:01:30.155 --> 00:01:32.358
-Yeah. Yeah.
No, totally.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:33.926
And, also, like, wear clothing.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.628
-You know?
'Cause I've just been, like,

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:38.130
basically, you know,
in underwear from like

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:42.034
here down 'cause Zoom is just...
It's been so nice.

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:45.338
It's been nice to, like,
see people and interact.

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:48.474
-I will say, when people ask me,
because I don't mind

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.576
talking to people on Zoom,
but one of the nice things is --

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.878
I don't get to actually see them
before the show.

00:01:52.878 --> 00:01:55.081
And it was so nice to be able
to go back in the dressing room

00:01:55.081 --> 00:01:57.083
and talk to you,
and so that's the part

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.351
I miss the most about Zoom.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.220
-Yeah, just, like, interacting
with human beings.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.620
-Yeah.
-Yeah, 'cause you can't crawl

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:03.490
through your camera.
-No.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.090
-Apple hasn't
done that for us yet.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.026
Which, honestly,
I really thought they would.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:07.993
-It's like, "Come on, guys.
Catch up."

00:02:07.993 --> 00:02:09.495
-I know.
I was like, "Hello?

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:10.929
Can you guys --"
-This was the year to do it.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:12.431
-"Can you...?"
-Speaking of --

00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:14.334
You were very
ahead of the curve.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.035
I want to applaud you.
-Oh.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:18.203
-Because last time
you were here, pre-pandemic...

00:02:18.203 --> 00:02:20.506
-Yeah.
-...we talked about how

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:23.542
you rented an RV.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:25.411
-And you drove across country.
-Yeah, I did.

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.180
My husband and I
and our dog Moose.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.217
I had to --
the show that I had done before,

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.485
"Tales of the City,"
was premiering

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.320
at the San Francisco
Film Festival.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.922
And we realized
we had about three weeks,

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.523
and so we had always
wanted to do that.

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:40.093
We had had a belated honeymoon.
We rented an RV.

00:02:40.093 --> 00:02:42.394
We drove there and back.
-Wow.

00:02:42.394 --> 00:02:44.063
-And that was --
I came on the show

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.198
right after that,
right after we got home.

00:02:46.198 --> 00:02:48.400
And funnily enough,
I was speaking to your producer

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.803
yesterday, and she was like,
"So let's talk about that."

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.305
And I was like --
Literally, my husband

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.473
was sitting next to me
googling RVs,

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:57.576
because "Flight Attendant,"
season two, shoots in L.A.,

00:02:57.576 --> 00:02:59.779
and we don't want to fly
with our dog,

00:02:59.779 --> 00:03:03.349
and so we're about to buy an RV
and do it again.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.218
-I see --
I'm a little bummed,

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.986
Because I had hoped
that you had bought an RV

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.955
before the pandemic.
'Cause I feel like you're in

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.524
a situation where you're gonna
be, like, buying Bitcoin now.

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:13.592
Right?
The RV, it must be a booming --

00:03:13.592 --> 00:03:16.128
-I just -- Look, you know,
nobody's perfect.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:17.997
-Right.
-Like, I'm honestly also upset

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:21.434
that I didn't invest in Oatly,
but, like, 2020 hindsight.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.901
You know?
-Yeah, right.

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:24.504
-So, like,
I'm definitely kicking myself

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.639
for both of those things.
But, um...

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.641
-But you're gonna
live that RV life again.

00:03:28.641 --> 00:03:29.876
-I'm still --
We're still gonna do it.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.177
You know?
-That's great.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.145
-I think he's, like,
on Facebook Marketplace, like,

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:35.681
negotiating with some woman
named Betty in Upstate New York,

00:03:35.681 --> 00:03:37.082
being like --
-Is your --

00:03:37.082 --> 00:03:39.051
I'm married to the negotiator
in our relationship.

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:40.954
Is your husband the negotiator?
-Oh, 1,000%.

00:03:40.954 --> 00:03:42.421
-Yeah.
-I'm the one, someone's like,

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:43.856
"I'll give it to you
for five times the price,"

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:46.192
and I'm like, "Sold! Great!
I'm so sorry.

00:03:46.192 --> 00:03:48.228
Do you also want me to, like,
pay you more

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:51.264
and, like,
dance and also apologize?"

00:03:51.264 --> 00:03:53.866
-Yeah.
-He's like, "What did you do?"

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.235
What do I --
He always laughs at me,

00:03:55.235 --> 00:03:57.536
because I say --
I get the saying wrong.

00:03:57.536 --> 00:03:59.371
I'm like, "It's a steal
at half the price."

00:03:59.371 --> 00:04:01.574
And he's like,
"Yes, it would be."

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.009
[ Both laugh ]

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:05.812
"But that's not
the actual saying."

00:04:05.812 --> 00:04:07.213
-Yes.
-So that's -- yeah.

00:04:07.213 --> 00:04:08.914
-It's nice to be married
to a negotiator.

00:04:08.914 --> 00:04:13.185
-It helps a lot, for sure.
-Congratulations on this show.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:14.354
-Thank you.
-Which I'm saying backstage

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.088
I feel like was a show
that showed up

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.857
at the perfect time for people
who are desperate

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:19.926
to watch something new,
and it felt very unique.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:22.661
And one of the things that seems
genuinely great about it

00:04:22.661 --> 00:04:26.198
is that you were very close
with the people

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:28.601
you worked on the show with
and very appreciative.

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:30.570
'Cause you started, stopped,
and started up again.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:34.273
-Yeah.
We got incredibly lucky.

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:38.511
It was also insanely --
It was, like, some crazy kismet.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.714
We literally had just wrapped
our fifth episode.

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:45.584
We did eight total.
So they were able to do post

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:47.754
on our first five
during the pandemic,

00:04:47.754 --> 00:04:49.855
totally remotely,
which was super wild.

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:52.124
We had, like, a few reshoots.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:55.061
But so many shows were getting
canceled left and right.

00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:59.465
Basically, HBO Max and Warner
kept saying, like, "Don't worry.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.467
We promise we'll let you
finish the season."

00:05:01.467 --> 00:05:03.769
Which even just knowing
throughout the pandemic --

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:05.204
no one knew
when it was gonna end --

00:05:05.204 --> 00:05:08.073
knowing that we had that to go
back to --

00:05:08.073 --> 00:05:10.376
And I'm super jaded,
and I didn't believe it

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:11.744
until we got there.
But we did.

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:15.715
We got to finish our season.
And we felt so lucky

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:18.183
'cause we had had all this time
shooting together already,

00:05:18.183 --> 00:05:21.120
so we created
this creative shorthand,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.022
and we had these relationships.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:26.425
We all, like, genuinely knew
and loved each other.

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:29.595
And so when we went back
under the umbrella of shooting

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:33.866
with these new COVID protocols,
we had, like, this --

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:38.070
You know, we had created this --
these friendships already,

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.273
and so it didn't
feel strange or scary.

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.275
Like, I mean,
we all were worried it would,

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:44.544
but then we got on set
with each other,

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:46.845
and everybody
just, like, jumped in.

00:05:46.845 --> 00:05:48.548
-And you managed to do --

00:05:48.548 --> 00:05:50.249
I guess Kaley
gets credit for this.

00:05:50.249 --> 00:05:53.652
You managed to do a wrap party
with social distancing.

00:05:53.652 --> 00:05:58.690
-Yes. Kaley refused to not
let us not have a wrap party.

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:03.262
I think it took us
like a year and a half

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.230
to shoot eight episodes.
And, you know,

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.466
we're not "Game of Thrones,"
so that was surprising.

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:09.702
-Right.
-And so, yes.

00:06:09.702 --> 00:06:11.837
We social-distanced.
We all wore masks.

00:06:11.837 --> 00:06:13.472
-And then, it seems the gifts,

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:15.508
the wrap gifts
are very unicorn-themed.

00:06:15.508 --> 00:06:17.676
-Yeah.
So I feel like I --

00:06:17.676 --> 00:06:19.545
I feel like I've always been
a unicorn lover,

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:23.315
but it really just --
I feel like I really, like,

00:06:23.315 --> 00:06:26.052
told the world this year
that that's inside.

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.953
I finally like -- I admitted it.

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:30.556
-It was a good year to, like,
admit a secret about yourself,

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:33.159
because so much was going on
that nobody could overreact

00:06:33.159 --> 00:06:34.660
to the fact
that you were a unicorn lover.

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:35.895
-I think so.
Yeah, I just -- I was like,

00:06:35.895 --> 00:06:37.029
"You guys, I love unicorns!"

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:39.632
And everybody was like,
"Okay, cool."

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.434
Yeah.
So, Kaley gave me my wrap gift,

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.002
which included something special

00:06:43.002 --> 00:06:44.937
and also
all of those unicorn things.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.472
-Yeah, it was really lovely.

00:06:46.472 --> 00:06:48.841
And it's such a good show.
-Thank you.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.710
-And it's so lovely
to see you again.

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:51.911
-It's so lovely to see you.

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:53.079
-And thank you for making
the time and coming here.

00:06:53.079 --> 00:06:54.914
-Thank you for having me.
-You guys,

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:56.582
"The Flight Attendant"
is available to stream now

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.918
on HBO Max. She's in it.
She's wonderful.

